ss or hay, we’d starve and waste away, no matter how much cellulose we ingested. --- ### In a nutshell | Horse | Human | |-------|--------| | Hindgut fermenter (cecum + colon) | Minimal hindgut fermentation | | Microbes convert fiber → energy + **synthesize all essential amino acids** from non‑protein nitrogen | Cannot synthesize essential amino acids; must obtain them from food | | Absorbs some amino acids from hindgut; recycles urea efficiently | No significant large‑intestine protein absorption | | Can thrive on high‑fiber forage with modest protein content | Needs a balanced diet with adequate complete protein | So, horses aren’t building massive muscles from
